Chapter: NetDriverSeamNoAv
  cites Net chapter NetDriver

 The control for net-driver-seam-bound, and the first exercise of the
 AV-bit refusal in anger. Same program, same card present, one register
 changed: RAH bit 31 clear, so the part has been given no address.

 The bind must refuse it and the seam must answer the NE2000 constant.
 A refusal that fabricated an address instead would leave every later
 stage looking healthy while the card filtered out the replies, which
 reads on the glass as a dead cable rather than as a wrong address.

Section: Judges

 The fallback address is written out here rather than taken from
 NetDriver. A test that imports its comparand from the chapter it is
 judging cannot fail when that comparand moves, and this arm asserts the
 seam DID answer this value, which makes the independence load-bearing in
 the other direction too.

  t-ne2k-mac : List Integer = [82, 84, 0, 18, 52, 86]

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

  bytes-of : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  bytes-of (l) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else bytes-of l (i + 1) n (acc & " " & show (list-at l i))

  mac-same : List Integer, List Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  mac-same (a) (b) (i) =
    if i >= 6 then True
    else if list-at a i /= list-at b i then False
    else mac-same a b (i + 1)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let card = net-driver-bring-up
    in let mac = net-driver-mac
    in let len = list-length mac
    in act
      print-line-uni ("bound card  : " & net-driver-card-name card)
      print-line-uni ("mac length  : " & show len)
      print-line-uni ("seam mac    :" & bytes-of mac 0 len "")
      print-line-uni ("is ne2k mac : " & yn (len == 6 & mac-same mac t-ne2k-mac 0))
    end
  end

